  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday morning through next Thursday)\nIssued at 336 PM EDT Fri May 8 2026\n\nA final push of showers and thunderstorms is expected Monday late in \nthe morning or early in the afternoon as a cold front sweep the \nstationary front out over the Atlantic. While severe weather is not \nexpected, a few thunderstorms could produce gust winds and frequent \nlightning. \n\nRain should clear the area Monday afternoon and high pressure will \nsettle in behind it. Cooler conditions will linger through next \nWednesday with highs in the mid 70s with lows in the mid 40s and low \n50s. Temps will heat up late next week as temps climb back into the \nlow to mid 80s. The rest of the week should be rain free, as the \nridge continues to build.",
